# 1. Application Concept

This is a live-streaming application.

The same application must allow authenticated users to:

* Watch live streams
* Browse currently live users
* Start their own live stream
* End their live stream
* View live stream information
* Participate in live chat
* View their profile
* Edit their profile
* View live history
* Manage settings

Any authenticated user can:

* Become a viewer
* Become a broadcaster

There should NOT be separate broadcaster and viewer applications.

---

# 2. Backend / Streaming Architecture

I do NOT have my own backend or streaming server.

Use managed services.

Recommended architecture:

```text
Flutter App
    |
    +---- Firebase Authentication
    |
    +---- Firestore
    |
    +---- Firebase Cloud Functions
    |
    +---- Cloudflare Stream
    |
    +---- HLS Video Playback
```

### Flutter

Responsible for:

* UI
* Navigation
* Camera/microphone access
* Video playback
* User interactions
* Chat UI
* Live controls

### Firebase Authentication

Responsible for:

* Registration
* Login
* Logout
* Authentication state
* User identity

### Firestore

Responsible for:

* User profiles
* Live stream metadata
* Live status
* Comments/chat
* Basic viewer information

### Firebase Cloud Functions

Responsible for:

* Secure server-side operations
* Cloudflare Stream API communication
* Creating/managing live inputs
* Protecting Cloudflare API credentials

### Cloudflare Stream

Responsible for:

* Live video ingest
* Video processing
* Live playback
* CDN delivery
* Optional recording

